	<div id="main"><h1>Governor's Executive Orders 2004</h1>
<div id="navcontainer">
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_001">Executive Order 04-01</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden establishes the Public Safety Officer Medal of Valor, and the Medal of Valor Review Board within the Department of Public Safety. (Feb. 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_002">Executive Order 04-02</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Feb. 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_003">Executive Order 04-03</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden establishes the Missouri Automotive Partnership. (Jan. 14)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_004">Executive Order 04-04</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden establishes the Missouri Methamphetamine Education and Prevention Task Force. (Jan. 27)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_005">Executive Order 04-05</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden establishes a Missouri Methamphetamine Treatment Task Force. (Jan. 27)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_006">Executive Order 04-06</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden establishes a Missouri Methamphetamine Enforcement and Environmental Protection Task Force to replace the Missouri Inter-Agency Clandestine Lab Task Force. (Jan. 27)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_007">Executive Order 04-07</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden establishes the Missouri Commission on Patient Safety and rescinds <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2003/eo03_016">Executive Order 03-16</a>. (Feb. 3)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2010/eo10_008">Executive Order 10-08</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_008"><strong>Executive Order 04-08</strong></a><br>Gov. Bob Holden transfers the Governor's Council on Disability and the Missouri Assistive Technology Advisory Council from the Department of Labor and Industrial Relations to the Office of Administration. (Feb. 3)<br>- Rescinded in part by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_006">Executive Order 06-06</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_009">Executive Order 04-09</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders vendors for the state to disclose services performed offshore. State agencies are restricted in awarding contracts to vendors performing services offshore. (Mar. 17)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_010"> Executive Order 04-10</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on May 24, 2004. (May 28)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_011"> Executive Order 04-11</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden declares a regional state of emergency and temporarily suspends certain regulations related to motor carriers due to severe weather in the State of Michigan and the need to repair electrical outages by various contractors, including a Missouri contractor. (May 28)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_012"> Executive Order 04-12</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden amends <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_010">Executive Order 04-10</a> and declares an emergency due to severe weather in all Northern and Central Missouri counties. (June 4)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_013"> Executive Order 04-13</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden declares June 11, 2004, to be a day of mourning for President Ronald Reagan. (June 7)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_014"> Executive Order 04-14</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden establishes the Missouri Emancipation Day Commission. (June 17)<br>- Superseded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2010/eo10_017">Executive Order 10-17</a><br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_015">Executive Order 04-15</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden declares a regional state of emergency and temporarily suspends certain regulations related to motor carriers due to lost electrical service in the St. Louis region. (July 7)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_016">Executive Order 04-16</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders a special census be taken in the City of Licking. (July 23)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_017">Executive Order 04-17</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden implements the Emergency Mutual Aid Compact (EMAC) agreement with the State of Florida to provide assistance in response to Hurricane Charley. (Aug. 18)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_018">Executive Order 04-18</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden accepts retrocession of federal jurisdiction over the St. Louis Army Ammunition Plant (SLAAP). (Aug. 25)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_019">Executive Order 04-19</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden implements the Emergency Mutual Aid Compact (EMAC) with the State of Florida, activates the EMAC plan, and authorizes the use of the Missouri National Guard in response to Hurricanes Frances and Ivan. (Sep. 10)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_020">Executive Order 04-20</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden re-establishes the Poultry Industry Committee. (Sep. 14)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_021">Executive Order 04-21</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders the creation of the Forest Utilization Committee within the Missouri Department of Conservation. (Sep. 14)<br>- Superseded and rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_023">Executive Order 04-23</a><br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_022">Executive Order 04-22</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders health care providers to limit influenza vaccinations to persons in high risk categories. The Missouri Department of Health and Senior Services is ordered to assess vaccine supply and convey the need assessment to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. (Oct. 25)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2005/eo05_011">Executive Order 05-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_023">Executive Order 04-23</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders the creation of the Forest Utilization Committee within the Missouri Department of Conservation and rescinds <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_021">Executive Order 04-21</a>. (Oct. 21)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_024">Executive Order 04-24</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden rescinds <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2003/eo03_015">Executive Order 03-15</a>. (Oct. 21)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_025">Executive Order 04-25</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden rescinds <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2003/eo03_027">Executive Order 03-27</a>. (Oct. 21)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_026">Executive Order 04-26</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden authorizes the Adjutant General to recognize Noncommissioned Officers with a First Sergeant's ribbon. (Nov. 1)</p>
<p><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_027"><strong>Executive Order 04-27</strong></a><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders state offices to be closed Friday, November 26, 2004. (Nov. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2004/eo04_028">Executive Order 04-28</a></strong><br>Gov. Bob Holden orders state offices closed on Monday, January 10, 2005, for the inauguration. (Dec. 6)</p>
</div>
